### gloss ser
to be (essentially or identified as); to be (in the passive voice sense); to exist, to occur; a being, organism; nature, essence; value, worth
### gloss ir
to go (away from speaker and listener); to be suitable or apt for its purpose, to match or suit well (of clothing); to head towards or lead to a place away from the speaker; to extend in time or space, from one point to another; to play; to approach or consider (something) from a specific angle, or to direct attention towards a particular goal; denotes an ongoing action with a sense of progression or movement through space or time, to go on (doing something), to carry on, to keep on; an action or process is beginning to occur or unfold, to grow (dark), get (cloudy)
### gloss estar
to be (have a temporary or permanent location in space); to be present; to be (denotes a copula, in a transient fashion); to be (auxiliary verb for the progressive/continuous aspect, preceding the gerund of the verb); to be in a state (in a passive voice sense); to be, stay (denotes a copula, in a transient fashion); to be (still); to be in a long-term state (in specific idioms)
### gloss haber
to have, forms the perfect aspect; to hold, to possess; to exist, there be, “there is”, “there are” (hay), “there was”, “there were” (hubo/había); to have to; to be necessary; asset; history; credit side
### gloss tener
to have, to possess; to have, to possess, to be (a condition or quality); to hold, to grasp; to contain, to hold (e.g. to “hold the power to”, “hold the key”, “hold a clue”, “hold the truth”, “have a hold on”, “hold in store”, “hold all the cards”, “hold in high regard”, etc.); to have, to feel (internally); to make to feel; to have (a measure or age); to have to
### gloss hacer
to do, perform, execute, carry out; to make; in various expressions about the weather; to release, to excrete; to prep, adorn, do (a body part); to make, to cause to be; to make, to cause to; task, action
### gloss decir
to say, to tell, to name, to mention; to pronounce, sound out; to say, opine; to say (of writing); to show, to demonstrate; to call; saying; idle talk
### gloss poder
to be able to, can; to be familiar with something, or with someone's personality; power (the ability to coerce, influence or control); proxy (written certificate of authority to act for another); authorization; possession, property
### gloss dar
to give, to give out; to hand over; to hit (from any distance); to hit oneself, bump into, crash into; to encounter, to find with effort; to emit; to produce; to perform
### gloss ver
to see, to spot; to see, to look at, to view (perceive); to see, to tell, to observe; to see, to check (verify); to watch; to look, to seem; to see oneself, to picture oneself; to find oneself, to be
### gloss casa
